<title>UK: Ghana cocoa purchases behind year earlier.</title>
<headline>Ghana cocoa purchases behind year earlier.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ghana cocoa purchases to the end of the seventh week of the 1996/97 season were a cumulative 149,906 tonnes compared with 208,658 tonnes at the end of the corresponding week of the year-earlier season.</p>
<p>The Ghana Cocoa Board said it purchased 14,455 tonnes of cocoa in the week ended November 28 compared with 21,327 tonnes in the eighth week ended November 30 of the year-earlier season.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
